ndGradient":null,"backgroundImageId":null,"backgroundImageUrl":null},"buttonOptions":{"backgroundColor":"#334BFA","fontColor":"#ffffff","borderRadius":6},"isFullWidth":false,"align":null}},"helpCenterName":"1inch.io - Help Center","footerLogo":"https://downloads.intercomcdn.com/i/o/zgn72x6y/784533/9c326d9c35e165b8919aec049238/d1701c7bb19e05a4ae219991e79df2d8.png","footerLogoHeight":"282","localisedInformation":{"contentBlock":{"locale":"en","title":"Content section title","withButton":false,"description":"","buttonTitle":"Button title","buttonUrl":""}}},"articleContent":{"articleId":"6200682","author":{"avatar":null,"name":"Anastasiia Pustovoitova","first_name":"Anastasiia","avatar_shape":"circle"},"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"A common question asked is, \u003cb\u003e\"Why should I use 1inch instead of a regular DEX Uniswap or Pancakeswap?\"\u003c/b\u003e","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":" ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"At first glance, the interface of 1inch Network looks very similar to alot of Decentralized Exchanges (DEXes) in DeFi; however, under the hood there are some powerful features to help users save money on swaps.","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":" ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"heading","text":"Efficient routing","idAttribute":"h_ab432d95f5"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"By design, 1inch uses a dynamic \"aggregation\" protocol. This differs significantly from the AMM protocols of individual DEXes. Instead of executing transactions, it finds the cheapest rate amongst a multitude of Dexes (including Uniswap and Pancakeswap), and submits the transaction through that DEX. This means that if Sushiswap has a more affordable rate than Uniswap, 1inch will do the work for you and route your swap through Sushiswap.","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":" ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"heading","text":"Transaction splitting","idAttribute":"h_9ecdd73fb4"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Transaction splitting is also another key component of how 1inch saves money for its users. If you were to make a swap on an individual DEX (like Uniswap), your trade could \u003ci\u003eonly\u003c/i\u003e go through one single liquidity pool. Therefore, as your trade size increases, a larger \u003ca href=\"https://help.1inch.com/en/articles/4585109-what-is-price-impact-vs-price-slippage-in-defi\"\u003enegative price impact\u003c/a\u003e will be incurred, resulting in unnecessary losses.","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":" ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"With 1inch, however, your single trade can be split up and routed through multiple liquidity sources! This minimizes the negative price impact and saves significant amounts of capital. ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":" ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"heading","text":"Gas optimization","idAttribute":"h_9d9530279b"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In addition to efficient routing and transaction splitting, 1inch also works to optimize gas fees. 1inch Network contributors continually update the protocol to enhance gas optimization, resulting in cheaper gas fees than most leading DEXes.","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":" ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Due to the protocol's efficiency, gas fees for smaller transactions are often cheaper than Uniswap, even if 1inch routes the transaction through Uniswap itself.","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":" ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"heading","text":"Fusion Mode","idAttribute":"h_6ce887f886"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"With \u003ca href=\"https://help.1inch.com/en/articles/6796085-what-is-1inch-fusion-and-how-does-it-work\"\u003e1inch Fusion\u003c/a\u003e, a new 1inch swap engine is introduced for filling and executing orders. It allows users to \u003cb\u003eswap at a competitive rate without needing native tokens for gas fees\u003c/b\u003e and seamlessly prevents front-running (MEV) attacks. In a general sense, it can be seen as a total overhaul of 1inch Network’s existing \u003ca href=\"https://help.1inch.com/en/articles/4656415-how-to-place-a-limit-order-on-1inch\"\u003eLimit order\u003c/a\u003e and aggregation protocols.","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":" ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Similar to a Classic swap, you first enter the token amounts that you want to swap. This designates you as the \"maker\". Once the order is placed, resolvers (takers) compete to fill your order and also cover any associated gas fees.","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":" ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"With all of these unique qualities combined, anyone who uses 1inch will \u003cb\u003esave substantial amounts of capital\u003c/b\u003e in comparison to using individual dexes like Uniswap or Pancakeswap.","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"paragraph","text":" ","class":"no-margin"},{"type":"subheading","text":"Questions, comments, concerns? Feel free to reach out to us in the Live Support Chat!","idAttribute":"h_827eef95d8"}],"collectionId":"2625609","description":"How 1inch Network will save you money when trading in DeFi","id":"5892916","lastUpdated":"Updated over a week ago","lastUpdatedDate":"2026-08-28T18:28:39Z","markdown":null,"relatedArticles":null,"targetUserType":"everyone","title":"Why is using 1inch better than a DEX (like Uniswap or Pancakeswap)?","showTableOfContents":true,"synced":false,"isStandaloneApp":false},"breadcrumbs":[{"url":"https://help.1inch.com/en/collections/2625609-getting-started-with-1inch","name":"Getting started with 1inch"}],"selectedReaction":null,"showReactions":true,"themeCSSCustomProperties":{"--body-bg":"rgb(255, 255, 255)","--body-image":"none","--body-bg-rgb":"255, 255, 255","--body-border":"rgb(230, 230, 230)","--body-primary-color":"#1a1a1a","--body-secondary-color":"#595959","--body-reaction-bg":"rgb(242, 242, 242)","--body-reaction-text-color":"rgb(89, 89, 89)"